From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: irisrun <irisrun@localhost>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 04:36:04 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/38] Edit text with the editing state Iris's host shares
 with UIKit

Iris's UIKit (OpenUIKit) edits text from the host's input method and keyboard
the same way, so the editing state moves to the IrisHost target in Iris's
runtimes/ios: the text with the marked text in it, as UITextInput has it,
the selection, and what commits, compositions, corrections and editing keys
do. Bindings still get the text without the marked text. A tap or Return
keeps the marked text the input method left, as UIKit does.
---
